  "summary": "LIVE READING (MEASURED, objectstack main 3054516e, examples/app-showcase booted with objectstack dev --seed-admin --no-watch on its own port and its own SQLite file, from a separate detached objectstack worktree, since removed). Requests were sent directly over HTTP and also through the REAL editor with a real MetadataClient over HTTP, in a one-off harness that was not committed. Q1, a draft-only parent: the console's request today, PUT /api/v1/meta/object/qa_sales_order with no query string and body {fields:{amount:{type:number,label:'Order amount'}}}, is answered 422 INVALID_METADATA with one issue at path 'name' ('Invalid input: expected string, received undefined', invalid_type). Afterwards the published read and /layers still answer 404, and the draft is unchanged and still in the ledger. NOTHING IS PUBLISHED. Through main's editor the banner reads 'Validation failed (1 issue).', not 'Saved.'. The 'name' issue is mapped onto the sub-form unchanged, so the edit is never saved and every retry sends the same stub. A publish-mode object write with no sharingModel is also refused (422, security-owd-unset), so the stub would be refused even if it carried a name. Q2, a published parent with a pending draft, saved through main's editor: the editor reads /layers (200), and the publish-mode PUT of effective plus the item answers 200. The edit WENT LIVE at once, with no publish by the author. The draft row was left as it was: its own edits (a renamed label and a new channel field) are kept, but it still holds the OLD amount label, so publishing that draft later puts the old label back. For triage's re-grade: the live server does not publish the stub, but on a published parent with a pending draft it does write live. FIX: EmbeddedItemEditor.doSave reads the parent's pending draft first, through the client's getDraft and extractDraftBody, both unchanged. When a draft exists, it splices the item into the draft and saves with { mode: 'draft' }. When there is no draft, it saves the published effective (or code) exactly as before. When neither can be read, it refuses with an error state built from the existing strings engine.edit.loadFailed and engine.form.notFound: nothing is sent and no 'Saved.' is shown. A failed draft read is the save's error (fail closed). The fix was measured live the same way. Draft-only: _drafts, ?state=draft, PUT ?mode=draft 200 'Saved.'; the stored row has the new amount label plus name/label/description/region, and nothing is published. Published+draft: PUT ?mode=draft 200; the draft keeps its rename and channel and gets the new label, and the published row is unchanged. Published, no draft: PUT with no query string 200, the same request as main's code. Neither: no PUT, 'Failed to load object/qa_live_f: (not found)'. The stored rows hold only authored keys: the client strips read decorations and the server strips served columns and nameField. The premise holds: the console sends the stub described. Only the card's 'says Saved' was the in-memory server's answer; live it is a 422.",
